unit REACH;
{ Reachability unit: names VCL and RTL API the original program also reaches.

  DCC's 16-bit linker keeps only reachable code, so the rebuild's library
  segments stay smaller than the original's until the program touches the same
  API (docs/segment-map.md, "The VCL segments are short by what the program
  reaches").  Every call here is plain Delphi 1 and pulls in code the original
  image already contains; nothing invents bytes. }

interface

procedure ReachMore;

